-- NEGATIVE fixture for the future D-CYCLE / D-RECURSIVE checks (spec §6.4.2,
-- §6.4.5).
--
-- p4: the cycle runs THROUGH A WHERE-LOCAL rather than between two top-level
-- names directly.
--
--     `the assessed value`  MEANS `adjusted`
--                           WHERE `adjusted` MEANS `the review value` PLUS 1
--     `the review value`    MEANS `the assessed value` MINUS 1
--
-- The interesting part is that the local is not a DRG node. Whatever the
-- exporter does with a WHERE binding -- inline it, hoist it, lift it -- the
-- cycle it participates in has to survive that transformation or the check
-- looks at the wrong graph.
--
-- On today's tree the emitted DRG IS cyclic here and the report is silent.
--
-- Expected after Phase 4: one D-CYCLE (or D-RECURSIVE, once the members
-- un-lift) over the two top-level names, with the local not listed as a member
-- because it is not a node.
--
-- Its companion cycle-p4-where-local-self.l4 is the case §6.4.5 CONCEDES is
-- invisible; read the two together.
--
--
-- PROVENANCE OF THIS HEADER. The .l4 source was typechecked (`l4 check`, clean)
-- when it was written on 2026-07-31, with a prebuilt CLI. The statements above
-- about what TODAY'S EXPORTER emits and reports are taken from spec
-- §6.4.2/§6.4.5's table and were NOT re-measured here: that session had no
-- build. Whoever wires these fixtures into jl4/tests/DmnExport.hs must MEASURE
-- the expectation rather than transcribe it.
-- NEVER added to `goldenSubjects`.

IMPORT prelude

§ `cycle through a where local`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the assessed value` MEANS
    `adjusted`
      WHERE
        `adjusted` MEANS `the review value` PLUS 1

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the review value` MEANS
    `the assessed value` MINUS 1
